<Project>

  <!--
    Imported into every project that installs Cap.Std, directly or through another package,
    and makes CS9057 an error there.

    A compiler loads an analyzer only when the compiler version the analyzer was built against
    is no newer than its own. When it is newer, the compiler reports warning CS9057 and builds
    without the analyzer, so every CAP rule, [assembly: CapabilityStrict] included, stops
    reporting and the build still succeeds. The analyzer in this package is built against the
    oldest compiler it supports (docs/analyzers.md gives the floor), so this should never fire;
    if it does, the project is on a compiler older than that floor, and it is better told so
    than left less contained than it believes.

    CS9057 is not specific to one analyzer, so this also fails a build for any other analyzer
    the project's compiler is too old to load. NoWarn with CS9057 turns the check off.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CS9057</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
